this video is sponsored by ubisoft let  me ask you a personal question  did you like breath of the wild okay  that was a rhetorical question because  of course you did but guess what  since you liked breath of the wild i  know you're going to love what i'm about  to talk to you about  introducing ubisoft's brand new open  world action adventure game called  immortals phoenix rising  i was lucky enough to be given the  opportunity to play this game on the  switch before its release by the buddies  at ubisoft and let me be the first to  tell you  i have genuinely enjoyed every minute of  gameplay  but let me explain to you exactly why i  have enjoyed this experience as much as  i have  as someone who initially was honestly a  bit on the fence about trying out the  game  i decided to give it a shot simply  because of the entire game  setup as in the in-game universe as in  greek mythology i don't know about you  but i am a sucker for a good delve into  the lore of the gods of olympus  and that's precisely what this game is  all about it's got all of the favorites  like zeus and athena and ares and  aphrodite and also the mythological  monsters like medusa or a manly minotaur  i personally feel like this focus on  mythology was a big reason behind the  huge successes of the franchises like  god of war so right off the bat i had a  good feeling about immortals  and once i started playing it's like  immediately i was  stunned it hits you as soon as you leave  the title screen with some charming  voice acting and character customization  you can look this way or that way or  have this voice or that voice  or this hair or no hair and once you  take your personalized hero  named phoenix with a y into the world  boy does it start opening up  right off the bat you're introduced to a  specific mechanic that i am personally  so glad to see again and that is the  ability to climb any surface at the cost  of stamina  i cannot stress how excited i am to see  this genius mechanic making its way into  more games because this is how you truly  unlock the feel of verticality in an  open world no i'm not overreacting as  you adventure through the game you  stumble across mysterious vaults that  feel  refreshingly familiar for fans of breath  of the wild that are full of puzzles and  monsters and normally reward your  perseverance with some sweet upgrades  like freaking wings did i mention the  wings yet because the wings are super  cool  there are tons of weapon and armor  upgrades defined in the game and another  awesome mechanic that again is just the  most  impressive thing in the world to me is  what i like to call transmogrification  no i didn't take that term from anywhere  why would you say that did you just find  a new piece of armor that stat wise you  should wear but you think it kinda makes  you look like a chump  well no sweat make that armor look like  this armor or hide it entirely  the world is yours to manipulate at will  speaking of which i mentioned earlier  that the story is non-linear right  because it is after you finish the  little beginning segment which is still  pretty open world  you can literally go anywhere at any  time  amazing and you know what's even cooler  immortals fenix rising is going to be  available on stadia xbox playstation the  nintendo switch which is what i'm  playing on right now  and pc so literally whatever you are  playing on on december 3rd you too  can experience this delightfully  charming adventure there are also some  pretty future-proof plans in place for  dlc  so along with the game there's an option  to purchase a season pass which includes  the next three narrative-based dlc packs  that will each include new  heroes and even branch into the world of  chinese mythology  and don't even get me started on chinese  mythology okay it's awesome but you want  to know what really puts the fun in  phenomenal  the combat if there's one thing most  will agree on with ubisoft games it's  the normally very fluid feeling combat  and immortals is no exception the setup  is that phoenix here can use three  weapons  a light weapon a heavy weapon and a bow  and you can switch in between them each  seamlessly in combat  there are also parry and perfect dodge  mechanics that enable you to slow time  for a bit to get some extra hits in on  an enemy and i personally like combining  this with some aerial combos for a lot  of damage the enemies are varied and  exciting to face off against  some of them will charge you head-on  some of them will throw things at you  spit things at you dive-bomb you from  the air  and the way that you deal with them is  completely up to you and i know what  you're thinking oh that's just some  basic combat setup that's been done a  million times before but can your basic  setup control an arrow as it flies  through the air  yeah i didn't think so imagine the  combat and puzzle mechanics that come  with that fun feature for spoiler  reasons i haven't even gone into what is  undoubtedly one of the coolest things  about the game  and that is the story which is  surprisingly much  better and deeper than you think given  the lighthearted nature of the art  direction and gameplay something that  took me a little bit to get used to  though that involves the narrative  is well narration which happens whenever  you do  pretty much anything you see prometheus  the titan is talking to zeus about the  story of phoenix that you are playing  through the entire time that you're  playing through it and like i said at  first i was a little put off by it but  it actually works out really well  and before too long become something  really fun that you look forward to  hearing whenever you face off against a  new enemy discover a new area or meet a  new face  the game also has some pretty great  quality of life features like a photo  mode  auto run and customizable controls i  think it's safe to say that i am a firm  believer in this game and i'm actually  very grateful to have been given the  opportunity to test it out and i  honestly think it's going to be a big  hit  it's got this laid back colorful  stylized eccentric vibe about it while  not doing away with some of the biggest  factors for what makes it a good game  also did i mention yet that the scenery  and lighting in this game is absolutely  gorgeous even on the nintendo switch and  with the game releasing on said switch  you can literally play immortals on the  go in the car  at your tv in bed or anywhere else but  if you had another platform in mind then  have no fear because like i mentioned  earlier this game is available on the  xbox one xbox series x ps4  ps5 google stadia the pc and of course  the nintendo switch  so whatever you're gaming on click the  link in the description below to start  your charming adventure in the world of  immortals phoenix rising today once  again huge thanks to the friends at  ubisoft for sponsoring this video and  letting me have fun with immortals  phoenix rising i truly hope that you  will too  as always thank you so much for watching  and if you do end up picking up the game  or just have a few general thoughts  about it let me know what you think in  the comments below  i hope you have a phenomenal rest of  your day and of course this is masentena  bennett signing out  peace  [Music]  now
 

